elopment life cycle. Much of the MIS research in the requirement analysis phase has been devoted to the topic of requirement determination and its verification. Alternative generation and evaluation is left, to a ...\n', 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'morphological analysis design alternatives systematic enumeration', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'morphological analysis design alternatives systematic enumeration':\n\n1. Morphological analysis (problem-solving) - Wikipedia\n   URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morphological_analysis_(problem-solving)\n   Morphological analysis or general morphological analysis is a method for exploring possible solutions to a multi-dimensional, non-quantified complex problem ...\n\n2. Morphological Analysis for Problem Solving | PDF - Scribd\n   URL: https://www.scribd.com/document/952055712/Morphological-box-Morphology-Ideas-Box-Zwicky-method\n   The method involves identifying the attributes of an object, defining variants for each attribute, and systematically combining them to generate new ideas.\n\n3. Morphological Matrix, then Scoring - Encyclopedia of Abstractions\n   URL: https://abstractopedia.org/mechanisms/morphological_matrix_then_scoring/\n   Rationale: The mechanism enumerates a Cartesian design space, removes inconsistent combinations, and quantitatively scores the viable candidates. Nearest ...\n\n4. Morphological prospection: profiling the shapes of things to come\n   URL: https://www.emerald.com/fs/article/11/6/4/80047/Morphological-prospection-profiling-the-shapes-of\n   The morphological method is predicated upon the systematic enumeration and examination of all conceivable possibilities within a “possibility space”,\n\n5. (PDF) Two frameworks of morphological analysis - Academia.edu\n   URL: https://www.academia.edu/42103967/Two_frameworks_of_morphological_analysis\n   The text identifies two basic morphological frameworks: abstractive and atomistic. Abstractive frameworks emphasize networks of implicational relations\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'TRIZ forced alternatives solution space exploration method', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'TRIZ forced alternatives solution space exploration method':\n\n1. Design exploration by using a genetic algorithm and the Theory ...\n   URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0926580522002278\n   The GA+TRIZ method promotes automated design exploration, investigation of unexpected solutions, and continuous interaction with the computational generating ...\n\n2. Case study: is there a space for TRIZ in the era of ChatGPT?\n   URL: https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/proceedings-of-the-design-society/article/case-study-is-there-a-space-for-triz-in-the-era-of-chatgpt/7173B2DD63E89B35D7D550679F24059D\n   27 Aug 2025 · This study investigates the integration of Large Language Models with the TRIZ to improve problem solving and innovation in industrial product ...\n\n3. TRIZ Tools to Space Policy and Strategy - spacestrategies.org\n   URL: https://spacestrategies.org/reports/triz-tools/\n   TRIZ (Theory of Inventive Problem Solving) is a comprehensive methodology and set of tools developed to tackle complex problems and promote innovation.\n\n4. TRIZ-GPT: An LLM-augmented method for problem-solving\n   URL: https://arxiv.org/html/2408.05897v1\n   12 Aug 2024 · The system is designed to identify one TRIZ contradiction pair in each round, which may limit designers' solution space. solution space ...\n\n5. Systematic Innovation and TRIZ: A Structured Approach to ...\n   URL: https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-92-0321-5_22\n   4 Aug 2026 · TRIZ is a scientific approach that provides engineers with principles and strategies able to find inventive solutions in a structured way, ...\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'multi-criteria decision analysis trade study alternative evaluation framework', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'multi-criteria decision analysis trade study alternative evaluation framework':\n\n1. Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis-Based framework for supply ...\n   URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1568494625011925\n   Dec 1, 2025 · This study proposes a comprehensive decision-support framework that integrates Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis (MCDA) with advanced sensitivity analysis techniques to assess the stability and reliability of alternative rankings under uncertainty.\n\n2. Multi-Criteria Decision Making (MCDM) Methods and Concepts\n   URL: https://www.mdpi.com/2673-8392/3/1/6\n   Jan 9, 2023 · Several authors have focused on multi-criteria decision-making methods in their research studies. This section aims to investigate the number of articles in this area to evaluate the importance of MCDM methods in different subject fields and gain an overview of the most cited MCDM methods.\n\n3. Multiple-Criteria Decision Analysis - an overview ...\n   URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/multiple-criteria-decision-analysis\n   Multiple criteria decision analysis (MCDA) refers to making preference decisions (e.g. evaluation and selection) over the alternatives available characterized by multiple attributes.\n\n4. Seeing the trade-offs: Evaluating visualizations for multi ...\n   URL: https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/14738716261457001\n   Jun 30, 2026 · Based on formative research with domain experts, we first characterize set comparisons in trade-off analysis. In two design workshops, we identify potential visualization solutions to support them.\n\n5. Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis Methods Comparison\n   URL: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/342710693_Multi-Criteria_Decision_Analysis_Methods_Comparison\n   Jul 1, 2020 · Multi-criteria decision analysis (MCDA) is widely used to solve various decision problems through alternative evaluation. MCDA methods can be used in every field that can define a...\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'design review forcing function alternative solution paths enumeration', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'design review forcing function alternative solution paths enumeration':\n\n1. Path Enumeration Solution for Evaluating Reliability, Based ...\n   URL: https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10922-024-09854-4.pdf\n   To the best of our knowledge, this is the first attempt to introduce a path enumeration and classification strategy that preemp-tively identifies the most reliable paths for VNR embedding.\n\n2. The ADR as a forcing function: how writing the record changes ...\n   URL: https://whychose.com/blog/adr-forcing-function-writing-changes-decision\n   Jun 12, 2026 · A forcing function is any structure that makes previously invisible gaps visible. The ADR template is a forcing function because it requires specific content in specific slots — and the inability to fill a slot is diagnostic, not just inconvenient.\n\n3. Analysis and Selection between Alternative Solutions\n   URL: https://sebokwiki.org/wiki/Analysis_and_Selection_between_Alternative_Solutions\n   This soft context view will provide additional criteria for the analysis process, which may become the critical issue in selecting between two equally effective solution alternatives.\n\n4. Efficient Enumeration of d-Minimal Paths Under Capacity ...\n   URL: https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11168226\n   Sep 17, 2025 · Beyond performance, our framework provides a canonical and reusable representation of all feasible d-minimal-path combinations, which can be leveraged in reliability analysis, path planning, or network design.\n\n5. Capturing alternative paths to improve design outcomes\n   URL: https://uxdesign.cc/capturing-alternative-paths-to-improve-design-outcomes-f85a9b66dadb\n   Jan 29, 2021 · In my experience, flow diagrams are critical to communicating design intent, especially around alternative paths in a flow. Creating flow diagrams early in the design process (as conceptual flows) helps you work out all needed elements in the experience.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': '"design space" "alternative solutions" "preserve disagreement" planning analysis', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': 'Search results for \'"design space" "alternative solutions" "preserve disagreement" planning analysis\':\n\n1. Engineering Design Process - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\n   URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/engineering/engineering-design-process\n   The engineering design process is defined as a series of steps that include defining the problem, generating alternative solutions, evaluating them, selecting a solution, detailing the design, defending the design, manufacturing and testing, evaluating performance, and preparing the final design report.\n\n2. SPACE MISSION ANALYSIS AND DESIGN - soleadventure.com\n   URL: https://soleadventure.com/digest/mL64A3603006/Space-Mission_Analysis_And-Design\n   Definition and Scope Space mission analysis and design refer to the systematic process of defining mission objectives, conceptualizing spacecraft and mission architecture, assessing technical feasibility, and planning operations. It integrates disciplines like aerospace engineering, astrodynamics, systems engineering, and mission planning to develop a comprehensive blueprint that guides the ...\n\n3. DesignerlyLoop: Forming Design Intent through Curated ...\n   URL: https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3800645.3812885\n   Jun 12, 2026 · For instance, Jamplate [96] employs graphic-based design templates (i.e., Five Whys, Competitive Analysis) to facilitate progressive, stepwise solution refinement and cognitive elicitation. While these graphical approaches enhance the editability and visibility of the design space, they primarily focus on the presentation of turn-based outputs.\n\n4. A Bio-Inspired Approach to Sustainable Building Design ... - MDPI\n   URL: https://www.mdpi.com/2313-7673/11/1/31?bm-verify=AAQAAAAN_____-7yNncB0ZwDRM1yuaXlvz8IGdBqENVZ38Ysq54NONYPe3h7qbQ0K5sYvFMidUBHNPVcRZ4y3ezxY1NBuoJqTc97W1RceFKcy-La_XtDCHkDrKKOS27Wprau65kuG509gYOlNQS0hbhvF8CjEkftUMI7Mk76tYZ0TEGGMHDf_E56SMVSplS6wkyp-r_bI1oMgP0Srss_bILxfv2-9sjfEhhfxZpre5lfyQIUYw00pGmVKY46u5LTPIVJAWa0GuY62cdw6j7m1w\n   Jan 2, 2026 · By merging bio-inspired optimization, intelligent encoding of discrete choices, and nature-informed decision analysis, this work not only offers a significant methodological contribution to building insulation system design but also exemplifies the effective translation of natural principles into sustainable engineering solutions.\n\n5. Full article: Accessibility, usability and universal design ...\n   URL: https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/09638288.2025.2491831\n   Apr 21, 2025 · Within urban planning, accessibility and usability efforts have historically had a certain element of co-creation through the establishment of “disability councils,” which were primarily tasked with tapping into the knowledge and experience of persons with impairments.\n', 'success': True}]
  librarian_finding: {'persona': 'Librarian researching design space exploration and alternative solution generation to counter context-loaded planning bias.', 'candidate': 'Morphological analysis (Zwicky method) systematically enumerates design alternatives by creating a matrix of problem dimensions and their variants, then combines them to explore the full solution space without anchoring bias.', 'solution_class': 'external-method', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morphological_analysis_(problem-solving)', 'is_this_a_graph': 'No; morphological analysis produces a Cartesian matrix of alternatives, not a graph structure, though results can feed graph-based trade studies.', 'effort_risk': 'Low effort, medium risk. The method is well-established and lightweight to apply, but requires discipline to avoid reverting to context-loaded shortcuts during enumeration.', 'rationale': 'Morphological analysis directly addresses the witnessed problem: it forces systematic exploration of all feasible combinations across problem dimensions, preventing shell-in-diff or hook-in-context anchoring. The matrix structure makes disagreement visible and preserves alternatives for trade-study evaluation.'}
  findings: [{'persona': 'os-infra-primitivist', 'candidate': 'File-system watch hook (CAP-222 macOS example) triggered by worktree state change, replacing shell-diff polling with OS-native FSEvents or inotify boundary enforcement.', 'solution_class': 'boundary-enforcement', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'CAP-222, CAP-254, does_the_platform_already_do_this', 'is_this_a_graph': 'yes', 'effort_risk': 'medium; FSEvents/inotify integration proven in CAP-222, but cross-platform abstraction and graph-node wrapping add surface.', 'rationale': 'OS already enforces file-change boundaries; leveraging native watch instead of shell-diff closure closes the witnessed 3-hour, 601-line hook cost by delegating to kernel.'}, {'persona': 'data-process-planner. I examine whether the input shape, schema, or lifecycle dissolves the problem before guards must catch it.', 'candidate': 'Require solution-class declaration in the FR brief itself, forcing authors to enumerate all candidate classes upfront.', 'solution_class': 'schema-data', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-806-author-sh-brief-preflight.md', 'is_this_a_graph': 'No. This is a schema and checklist change to the FR authoring contract, not a graph-based process.', 'effort_risk': 'Low effort, medium risk. Checklist addition is cheap; risk is adoption friction if authors resist upfront enumeration.', 'rationale': 'The witnessed incidents show authors ship solutions matching their loaded context (shell, hooks) without exploring alternatives. Forcing solution-class enumeration in the brief—before planning—closes input closure and prevents the planner from inheriting blind spots. FR-806 precedent shows this pattern works.'}, {'persona': 'yamlgraph-native-planner', 'candidate': 'Use research-route graph (FR-890 closed-input alternatives route) to fan-out orthogonal planner personas across solution classes, reducing findings into deterministic alternatives table instead of loading author context.', 'solution_class': 'graph-pipeline', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-890, research-route (examples/demos/research-route/graph.yaml), corpus-census (examples/demos/corpus_census/graph.yaml)', 'is_this_a_graph': 'research-route: load problem brief, collect known graph task shapes, fan out to orthogonal planner personas, reduce findings into deterministic alternatives table.', 'effort_risk': 'low/medium: graph skeleton exists; planner personas need authoring but map-reduce pattern is proven in corpus_census and cap_journey_census.', 'rationale': 'Witnessed incidents show author context bias (shell→shell, hooks→hooks). research-route pattern directly addresses this by fanning out independent personas across solution classes, ensuring OS-permissions and other alternatives surface deterministically without author-loaded context steering the result.'}, {'persona': 'Subtractionist: I prefer deletion, scope reduction, or explicit non-goals over automation when they fit better.', 'candidate': 'Delete the requirement to auto-propose solution classes from loaded context (shell→shell, hooks→hooks). Instead, enforce a mandatory planning phase that queries all seven solution classes—os-permissions, process-boundary, schema-data, graph-pipeline, subtraction, external-method, boundary-enforcement—before committing to one.', 'solution_class': 'graph-pipeline', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-806-author-sh-brief-preflight.md, CAP-248-research-sole-route-closed-input-alternatives, scripture-key: ask_before_generate', 'is_this_a_graph': 'Yes. The planning phase must enumerate all solution classes as a closed-input graph traversal, not a daemon or open-ended search.', 'effort_risk': 'Medium effort, low risk. Adds one planning graph node; reuses existing capability registry and sole-route pattern from FR-767 and CAP-248.', 'rationale': 'The witnessed incidents (2026-08-25) show that context-loaded solutions blind planners to available alternatives. A mandatory enumeration graph closes the input space and prevents the 601-line hook anti-pattern by forcing consideration of os-permissions and other classes upfront.'}, {'persona': 'Librarian researching design space exploration and alternative solution generation to counter context-loaded planning bias.', 'candidate': 'Morphological analysis (Zwicky method) systematically enumerates design alternatives by creating a matrix of problem dimensions and their variants, then combines them to explore the full solution space without anchoring bias.', 'solution_class': 'external-method', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morphological_analysis_(problem-solving)', 'is_this_a_graph': 'No; morphological analysis produces a Cartesian matrix of alternatives, not a graph structure, though results can feed graph-based trade studies.', 'effort_risk': 'Low effort, medium risk. The method is well-established and lightweight to apply, but requires discipline to avoid reverting to context-loaded shortcuts during enumeration.', 'rationale': 'Morphological analysis directly addresses the witnessed problem: it forces systematic exploration of all feasible combinations across problem dimensions, preventing shell-in-diff or hook-in-context anchoring. The matrix structure makes disagreement visible and preserves alternatives for trade-study evaluation.'}]
